From: Zhiyi Zhang <zzhang@codeweavers.com>
Subject: [PATCH] jscript: Support Unicode characters in identifiers.

Backported from WineHQ commits fbd19baa4f and 20e2458ab3 (wine-11.16,
both by Zhiyi Zhang) without code changes. The first moves keyword
lookup out of keyword parsing so the second can reuse it.

Identifiers may now contain Unicode letters and the other characters
ECMA-262 5th edition 7.6 allows, plus a few categories Windows also
accepts. Scripts that use a CJK punctuation mark such as U+3001 in an
identifier failed to parse, which stopped an application that loads
such a script at start-up.

